33,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,May,,"It turns out some of our ""innovations"" were tried years ago. Some worked, some were just abandoned for no good reason.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"How charming. Meanwhile, I've found that our ""available"" staff are essentially ghosts. We are running on fumes and overtime.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That's interesting. I found that the delays aren't where people complain most. The real time-loss is in the connections, not the crowds.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh dear, it seems we have some worries. I found that some approvals are quite a tangle, and the old tunnels are full of surprises.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings are troubling. We are paying far too much to contractors, and our capital balances are not as flexible as we hope.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, if we are running on fumes, we shouldn't pick a plan that requires a massive staffing surge without a proven model.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. Any plan that assumes we can simply ""add a few more runs"" without adding people is a fantasy.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, if we focus on the connection points rather than just adding more trains, we might solve the time-loss without needing more staff.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Midori. We should choose the path that avoids the pre-war shells and the complicated committee approvals.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,I must caution against any plan with high upfront contractor costs. We cannot afford to increase our long-term liabilities further.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,I'm seeing a pattern. We keep trying to expand when we should be refining what we already know works from the pilots.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I'm not against expansion, provided the expansion doesn't come at the cost of a crew member's sanity.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"If we can target the specific bottlenecks in the journey audits, we can improve the passenger experience without overextending the staff.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,Let us be gentle with our workers and our budget. A plan that is easy to approve and easy to build is the kindest choice.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. A sustainable plan is one that doesn't create a debt trap for the next five years.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,pass,May,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
