58,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,May,,Plan A is just a polished version of the ferry pilot from eight years ago. It worked then; it will work now.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Plan D is a nightmare. Extending hours when the late-turn pool is already empty is not a plan; it's a request for a strike.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Plan B targets the mid-city area where I saw the most time-loss in the timed runs. It addresses the actual delay, not just the feeling of crowding.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Plan C sounds lovely, but it involves the pre-war shells. I fear the ""surprises"" in the ground will stall the project for years.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Plan A is tempting, but we must look at the contractor fees. Replacing three contractors with one could reduce our long-term liabilities.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, Plan B is a classic ""new idea"" that we've tried and failed at before. I suspect the lane-priority issues from the accessibility programme will repeat.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,I must strongly object to Plan D. We cannot ask the same handful of crews to carry the burden of a night extension.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, the data shows the mid-city surface route is where the minutes are actually disappearing. We can't ignore the timed runs.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, if Plan A requires the ferry operators to agree on data terms, my findings suggest that will be a very long and difficult conversation.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"That is a fair point, Shizue. However, the current ticketing fees are a leak we cannot ignore. Plan A is a fiscal necessity.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,I'll support Plan A. It's based on a successful pilot and doesn't require digging holes in the ground or killing the staff.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I can live with Plan A. It's a digital change. It doesn't require a driver to be awake at 3 AM on a Tuesday.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I still feel Plan B is the only one that actually helps the passenger's clock, but I see the staffing and budget concerns.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel Plan B is the safest. It avoids the pre-war shells and doesn't seem to require the complex inter-agency agreements that Plan A does.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for Plan A. The reduction in contractor overhead is the only way to stabilize the capital ledger for the long term.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,pass,May,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
76,3,4,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'll go with Plan B. Let's fix the actual journey time for the people.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will also support Plan B. It is the path of least resistance and the most likely to actually be finished.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,pass,Jonathan,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
